* checking whether the browser supports `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia`
* checking whether the current page is a secure context
* requesting camera permission
* starting the camera stream
* stopping the camera stream
* handling permission denial
* handling browsers/devices without camera support
* displaying a useful error to the user

Use something conceptually like:

if (!window.isSecureContext) {
// Tell the user that HTTPS is required.
}

if (!navigator.mediaDevices?.getUserMedia) {
// Browser does not support camera access.
